SUMMARY:Negri-Nepote Grasslands
DESCRIPTION:We’ll search for migrants and returning grassland birds at this hidden gem. This restored grassland hosts a good variety of species including wetland species in the vernal ponds\, American Kestrel\, Eastern Bluebird and other thrushes\, sparrows\, and early warblers. Be prepared for three hours of walking over flat terrain. Muddy conditions are possible. We’ll also spend a little time looking at butterflies and dragonflies. There are no restrooms on site. Led by Christopher Daly and Carole Hughes. \nCOST: $20 Members\, $25 Non-members \nWEATHER & TRANSPORTATION: Please arrive at the appointed time. Be sure to check the forecast in advance and dress in layers appropriate for prevailing weather conditions. We sometimes bird in the rain\, so bring rain gear if warranted. Transportation during the field trip is by private vehicle (be sure you have enough gas). Most trips involve some amount of walking\, sometimes through muddy or sandy terrain. \nCANCELLATION: NJA/CMBO programs require a minimum number of registrants to run\, five days in advance of the start of the tour but are seldom cancelled. If we do cancel\, due to lack of participation\, severe weather\, or unforeseen circumstances\, we notify all participants in advance\, and all are eligible for a full credit or refund. Participants may cancel without penalty if greater than 30 days in advance. Cancellations 10 to 30 days in advance may be subject to a 25% service charge. No refunds or credits for cancellations less than ten days in advance unless due to health emergencies. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/negri-nepote-grasslands-5/
LOCATION:Negri-Nepote Native Grassland Preserve\, 260 Skillmans Lane\, Franklin Township\, NJ\, 08873\, United States
CATEGORIES:All Things Birds,Bird Walk,Birding
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Spring-Birding-at-Hawk-Rise-Sanctuary.jpg
GEO:40.4749155;-74.5253597
